--- body ---
## Context
`erg migrate` currently only converts legacy `Status:` headers to `Closed:`
form inside ticket files. Old projects may also have stale layout artifacts
from earlier erg versions: a `tickets/tools/` directory with the Go source
tree, a `tickets/FORMAT.md` (superseded by spec-erg-v1.md), an `archive/`
folder that was renamed to `closed/`, and missing AGENTS.md / spec files that
`erg init` now unpacks. There is no single command to bring an old install
fully up to date.

`erg migrate` should grow into that command: idempotent, safe (dry-run first),
covering both file-content migration and directory-layout migration.

## Actions
1. Add layout migration steps to `cmdMigrate` (run after the existing
   Status-header rewrite):
   a. If `tickets/tools/` exists, remove it with a confirmation message.
   b. If `tickets/FORMAT.md` exists, remove it (content is in spec-erg-v1.md).
   c. If `tickets/archive/` exists and `tickets/closed/` does not, rename it.
   d. Run the equivalent of `erg init` to unpack current AGENTS.md,
      spec-erg-v1.md, integration.md (refreshing stale copies).
2. Add `--dry-run` flag: print what would change without touching the filesystem.
3. Print a per-step summary: "removed tools/", "refreshed AGENTS.md", etc.

## Test
Create a temp dir with the old layout (tools/, FORMAT.md, archive/).
Run `erg migrate --dry-run` — must list all planned changes, touch nothing.
Run `erg migrate` — must apply all changes; re-run must be a no-op.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg migrate --dry-run` lists planned changes without modifying anything
- [ ] `erg migrate` removes tools/, FORMAT.md; renames archive/→closed/; refreshes init assets
- [ ] Re-running `erg migrate` on an already-migrated project is a no-op
- [ ] Existing Status-header migration still works
- [ ] `make test` passes
